### Validation Summary
- All 4 scripts run cleanly end-to-end without errors
- Replication: all 12 coefficients match original within 0.0005
- Extension data: 378 rows, 126 counties × 3 years, no missing core data
- Merged data: 1,832 rows (1,454 original + 378 extension)
- VCA adoption: 30 counties verified against CA SoS

### Key Findings
1. The null partisan effect of VBM holds through 2024 (coef = 0.004, SE = 0.003)
2. Turnout effect persists (~1.3pp) but attenuated post-2018 (COVID confound)
3. Clean event study: no pre-trends for either outcome
4. Results robust to excluding 2020

